<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Mudhol State</h1><p class="st-meta">1465 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Mudhol</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Deccan state of the Ghorpade family, Maratha chiefs who served the Bijapur Sultanate, and the source of the Mudhol hound.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghorpade">Ghorpades</a> of Mudhol were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> military chiefs who held Mudhol as a fief of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bijapur-sultanate">Bijapur Sultanate</a>; family tradition places the grant in the 15th century. The register's start date follows that tradition.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In the 17th century the Mudhol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghorpade">Ghorpades</a> remained loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a> and opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>, who killed Baji Ghorpade of Mudhol in 1664. Later the family held its lands under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a> and, from 1818, under British protection in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-maratha-country">Southern Maratha Country</a>. Its rulers promoted the lean Mudhol hound, a sight-hound now used by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-army">Indian Army</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Mudhol merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948 and was transferred to Mysore, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, in 1956. It is in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagalkot-district">Bagalkot district</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mudhol-state.jpg" alt="Mudhol State" width="320" height="189"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mudhol_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1465 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mudhol</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Baji Ghorpade</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kannada, Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mudhol</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1706&amp;focus=mudhol-state" aria-label="Mudhol State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6731 1571 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mudhol State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7051 1827L7364 1601M7051 1827L7364 1602M7051 1827L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7051 1827h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7051 1827h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mudhol. <a href="/atlas?year=1706&amp;focus=mudhol-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
